
\mytriangle{red} Here you can learn how to carry out algebra with lists:
  \begin{solutionbox} \begin{center}\bf{List Algebra with Casio fx-9750GII}\end{center}
\begin{center}To calculate for example List1$\wedge$ List2\end{center}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\protect\circled{\color{white}\arabic*}]
\item \begin{bf}Step one:\end{bf}   Enter the data: start the calculator and press \keystroke{menu} and the key \keystroke{2} to access the list menu (stat). You will follow all the steps on this menu. Type the List 1 and List 2 values.
 \item \begin{bf}Step two:\end{bf} In menu 1, press the \keystroke{OPTION} key and then the List option (key \keystroke{F1}). Now press the key \keystroke{1} to then pressing the power key \keystroke{$\wedge$} and again the \keystroke{OPTION} key and List now 2. 
  \item \begin{bf}Step three:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{EXE} and a List will appear populated with the result of List1$\wedge$List2 done row by row.
    \item \begin{bf}Step four:\end{bf} You can save this as List 3 by pressing \keystroke{\ce{->}} and \keystroke{OPTION} List 3
 \end{enumerate}
\end{solutionbox}

